   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing region by region.\n\n- **Pyrazine core:** the ring carries a primary carboxamide (C(=O)NH2) on one carbon and an NH\u2013aryl group on the adjacent carbon. The carbon across the ring from the carboxamide-bearing carbon carries the piperidine nitrogen, and the remaining ring carbon is CH.\n- **Piperidine on the pyrazine:** the piperidine N is attached to the pyrazine. Its 3-position carries a 3-methyl-2-oxoimidazolidin-1-yl group, drawn with a bold wedge.\n- **Stereocentre:** I worked out the chirality from the wedge geometry. With H pointing away, the neighbours run clockwise as ring CH2 (C2), then ring C4, then the imidazolidinone N. That gives `[C@H]` when written in the order `C[C@H](N\u2026)CC`.\n- **Aryl linker:** the NH connects to a para-phenylene, which is bonded to C4 of a 4-methylpiperidine. That piperidine nitrogen is acylated.\n- **Chain and E3 ligand:** the acyl group continues as C(=O)CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013NH. The NH is attached to position 4 of an isoindoline-1,3-dione. Its ring nitrogen bears a 2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl group. That carbon is a stereocentre by connectivity but is drawn with plain bonds, so it gets no stereo label.\n\nSMILES: NC(=O)c1nc(N2C[C@H](N3CCN(C)C3=O)CCC2)cnc1Nc1ccc(cc1)C1(C)CCN(CC1)C(=O)CCOCCNc1cccc2c1C(=O)N(C1CCC(=O)NC1=O)C2=O\n\nChecking the string against the drawing, the pyrazine is written as c1(C(N)=O) next to the NH-aryl carbon and N, with the piperidine-bearing carbon and CH on the other side. The pyrazine ring in the final line is `c1nc(N\u2026)cnc1N\u2026`, which puts the carboxamide carbon next to a ring N and the NH-aryl carbon. In the drawing the carboxamide carbon is bonded to the NH-aryl carbon and to a ring N, and the NH-aryl carbon is bonded to the other ring N. This matches the final string."
